		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3949&amp;p=30576#p30576"><![CDATA[
You can't flash the OpenGD77 firmware with any other tool than the one we're providing (CPS (Windows onyl) or the python script).<br>It's not possible to make a backup of the MCU without flashing the OpenGD77 firmware first, hence no more genuine firmware.<br>It's not possible to get radio model while in bootloader mode. Simply, if you flash the wrong firmware, it will remain in bootloader mode (with Red/Green leds flashing).<br>The Flash backup feature is for the external flash chip, not the MCU. But you need to make a backup after you get the firmware installed, because there are few sensitive data that you maybe need in the futur (like if you want to get back to manufacturer firmware).<br>Also, make a backup of the calibration (same window in the OpenGD77 CPS).<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Wed Apr 03, 2024 2:57 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
